  "caption": "Figure 1: Diagram of DeepCCG’s training routine. At time j the learner is given a sample of data Dj and has a memory set of stored datapoints Mj . The memory is split into the replay data Rj and the rest Mj/Rj . Learning happens by taking a gradient step on the parameters of the embedding function ϕ using a conditional marginal likelihood function over Dj and Rj , where Mj/Rj is used to induce a posterior over the means of the per-class Gaussians and so define the conditional marginal likelihood function used. Therefore, training aims to move the data points into per-class clusters, by drawing the embedded examples of Dj and Rj towards their own class means and away from the other class means, as shown in the embedding space diagram in the figure.",
